## Context

Child of 0245 (trace-doctor phase 5 targeted A/B), itself a child of
tracker 0236. This mirrors the 0315 split: 0315 landed the
pre-registration (interventions, metric definitions, decision rule,
red-first `trace_ab_decision.py`, gaze convergence flag default off);
the live A/B arms and the verdicts stay on 0245 because they are
author-scheduled operations that burn real tokens (measure A: paired
Sonnet-main replays; measure B: a live convergence-flag nightbeat week).

This child delivers the **offline tooling** those arms will consume:
the harvest CLI that computes the pre-registered metrics from cached
census + join inputs, the measure-A replay runbook, and the
pre-registered measure-A replay sample (deterministic selection, no arm
data). It writes no verdict and flips no flag.

## Relevant files

- `docs/trace-ab-2026-06.md` — pre-registration (0315); this ticket adds
  the measure-A sample list and the replay runbook, and leaves the
  measure-B week TODO(0245) placeholder untouched
- `scripts/trace_ab_decision.py` — `decide()` / `filter_window()`, reused
  by the harvest CLI (import only, no edit)
- `scripts/trace-pr-join.py` — `project_to_repo()` / `collect_pairs()`
  reused by the harvest CLI (import only, no edit); its cache
  `docs/trace-pr-join-2026-06.csv` is the join input
- `scripts/trace-stats.py` — census columns the harvest reads
  (`cost_usd`, `date`, `pr_numbers`, `verify_gaze_skills`); import only,
  no edit
- `docs/trace-counterfactuals-2026-06.md` — guardrail baselines
  (REROLL/PR 33/112, ESCALATE 18)

## Actions

1. `scripts/trace_ab_harvest.py` — pure, offline harvest CLI. argparse
   (no hardcoded paths), logging not print, Python 3.10+ builtin
   generics. Reads a census CSV and the join cache CSV, takes explicit
   `--window` dates, computes the pre-registered metrics
   (`cost_per_merged_pr`, `cost_per_cycle`, `reroll_per_pr`,
   `escalate_count`), and routes them through `decide()` / `filter_window()`
   from `trace_ab_decision.py`. Reuses `project_to_repo` / `collect_pairs`
   from `trace-pr-join.py`. Zero LLM calls, zero network, additive only —
   no edits to trace-stats.py / trace-hypotheses.py / trace-pr-join.py.
2. `docs/trace-ab-2026-06.md`: pre-register the measure-A replay sample
   with a deterministic selection rule (chosen ticket IDs, PR numbers,
   replay base SHAs) and add a short measure-A replay runbook (procedure,
   not a framework). Leave the measure-B week TODO(0245) placeholder as
   is — week selection is the author's call.
3. Log note to 0236: scaffolding landed; live arms remain on 0245.

## Test

- Red first: `tests/test_trace_ab_harvest.py` (fast tier, pure Python,
  no heavy deps). Fixtures use the phase-4 guardrail baselines verbatim
  (REROLL/PR 33/112, ESCALATE 18) and map computed metric values to
  adopt/reject verdicts through the harvest path
  (`compute_metrics` → `decide`).

## Invariants

- Zero LLM calls, zero network in the harvest CLI
- No trace content in outputs (aggregates and PR numbers ok)
- Existing census/join/hypotheses scripts untouched (import/reuse only)
- No verdict written; no B-arm data collected; the convergence flag
  stays default off
- Verdicts, when the arms run on 0245, come only from the pre-registered
  metrics — this tooling computes them, it does not shop for new ones

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `scripts/trace_ab_harvest.py` computes the pre-registered metrics
      from cached census + join inputs and routes them through
      `decide()` / `filter_window()`, offline and zero-LLM
- [ ] `tests/test_trace_ab_harvest.py` red-first tests pass, fixtures use
      the 33/112 REROLL and 18 ESCALATE baselines verbatim
- [ ] `docs/trace-ab-2026-06.md` carries the measure-A replay sample
      (deterministic rule + ticket IDs, PR numbers, base SHAs) and the
      replay runbook; measure-B TODO(0245) placeholder untouched
- [ ] Tracker 0236 log notes the scaffolding landing
- [ ] `make check` passes
